WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.369
-Welcome back
to "Late Night," everybody.

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.469
We are here with Leslie Jones.
-Yes!

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:04.604
-This is very exciting.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.806
You are -- starting tomorrow...
-Yes.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.975
-...you are hosting
"The Daily Show" for 3 nights.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:11.744
Are you excited to take on
this challenge?

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:13.179
-Yeah, I'm excited
that they don't know

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.682
what they're getting into.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.216
-I'm thrilled. I'm looking
forward to seeing it.

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:20.152
-I'm just -- I just want to
see what I'm-a do.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:21.321
-Yeah.
-Well, I mean --

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.922
-I mean, you've been behind
a desk before.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.558
Obviously, you did a lot of
stuff at "Weekend Update."

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.259
You've hosted before.
You've filled in for Ellen.

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:28.260
-Mm-hmm.
-So I think it ticks

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:29.562
a lot of boxes.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.130
And obviously, that staff is
still there in place.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.498
They're talented people.
-They're great, too.

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.467
They're actually awesome.
They've been very helpful.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:39.105
They've, you know, given us
great options and ideas

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.706
and being very supportive.

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:42.241
-Was there anything you
brought in where you said,

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:43.409
"Hey, I want to address
stories like this?"

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.811
-Yes. Yes.
There's a line of things

00:00:45.811 --> 00:00:47.947
I'm going to --
I can't tell you,

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.515
but, you know,
it's going to be good.

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:50.716
It's going to be good.

00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:52.785
We're going to be touching
some<i> subjects.</i>

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:54.119
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:56.589
-I'm very much looking
forward to the next 3 nights.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:59.158
It's also Oscars season,
and I do enjoy talking to you

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:01.694
about the media you've consumed
over the course of the year.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.028
-Yes.
-Are there any movies

00:01:03.028 --> 00:01:04.263
you're rooting for,
any movies you loved this year?

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:05.531
-You know what's so crazy?

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:08.000
Like, they were asking me that,
and I was like,

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.802
"Oh, my God, what movies?"

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:12.004
It's weird. This is so random.

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:13.640
"The Menu."
-"The Menu?"

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.973
[ Cheering ]

00:01:14.973 --> 00:01:18.711
We have "Menu" fans here.
-Yo, yo, have y'all seen that?

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:19.712
[ Audience shouts "Yes" ]

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.913
-Look at this.
-Okay.

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:23.917
First of all,
the title is very misleading.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.986
So I thought it was going to be
about a chef that they was

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:30.122
trying to bring back,
and, like, he was old.

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:32.625
He went and lived on an island
and started cooking.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.993
And the girl,
they was going to go over

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:35.327
there and get him
and bring him back.

00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:37.330
-I mean I do -- that movie
sounds awesome, too.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.899
-Yeah, but that's not what
happened on "The Menu."

00:01:40.899 --> 00:01:45.271
It was like, oh, hell no!

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.706
And there was no Black people
in that movie.

00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:49.108
-And there were no Black people
in that movie.

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:51.310
-Because don't no Black people
go to no island

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.879
and eat like that.

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:56.015
It was like, "So it's just
exclusive? Oh, no.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.718
So I can't use my phone?
Oh, no, no."

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.853
-So if I told you
there was a great restaurant

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:02.622
I wanted to take you to,
but we had to take a ferry

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.590
to get there, you would be --
that would be a hard no for you?

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.092
-Do you actually think
I'm-a to believe

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.626
another White person
and get on a boat?

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:10.663
[ Audience laughs ]

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:16.902
Fool me once, my fault.
Fool me twice...

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:18.237
[ Audience laughs ]

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:20.105
-I should note that one
of our writers, Seth Reese,

00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:21.707
co-wrote that movie.
-Really?

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:23.142
-Yeah, "The Menu."
A "Late Night" writer.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:25.278
-It was really -- I hope he
gets some -- some love for it,

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:26.412
some recognition for it.
-I think he's already

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:29.281
gotten more than enough
personally but --

00:02:29.281 --> 00:02:31.417
-You know, you've always been
kind of a super hater.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.419
-I mean -- I -- Thanks.
It's very nice of you to say.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.922
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.223
I think the last time
you were here,

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.725
I had not watched "Euphoria."
You had.

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:41.494
You love "Euphoria."
I've watched it now.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:42.995
I'm totally on board.
So I get it.

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:44.697
-Do you get it now?
-I get it now.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.267
-But, like, how much of a nerd
are you now?

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.268
Because, like, I was a complete
nerd after I watched that.

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:52.137
I was like, "Oh, I was a goody
two shoes in high school."

00:02:52.137 --> 00:02:53.472
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:56.709
-They are doing stuff I didn't
do until I was, like, 37.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.444
-Yeah.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.446
-I took --
I hope I'm not overreacting.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.848
I took my three kids after I saw
it, and I put them in a cabin

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:03.849
in the woods.
They're still there.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:05.584
-Yeah, exactly. Exactly.

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:08.220
-I'm like, you're not
allowed to be around other kids.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.791
-No, not them kids.
Not them kids.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.993
-Those kids, they're --
-Man. Ah, man.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.728
Ah, man. Ah, man.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.364
That one scene where Rue tore
the door down --

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.798
-Yeah.
-I was like, "Oh, my dad --

00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:21.801
my dad would have been, like,
calling the funeral homes

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:27.773
like, "So how long
can you get a coffin

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:29.174
because I'm about
to kill this girl.

00:03:29.174 --> 00:03:33.546
She just -- she just broke
a door in my house."

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.680
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.515
-I like that of all the
terrible things

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:38.784
they do on that show,
the line that would cross

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:40.853
for your dad
is a door was broken.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.254
-Yes. Thank you!

00:03:42.254 --> 00:03:45.524
Because first of all, these
kids, they just -- you know,

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:49.562
kids is just -- they just water
it down from the generations.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.497
So it's like,
you think I don't want --

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.599
my mom would be like, "Drugs?!

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.701
You think I don't want
to be high, Leslie?!

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:59.672
You think I don't want
to be high?!

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.607
Get yo ass in the kitchen!"

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:03.509
[ Audience laughs ]

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.810
-That's a good way
of looking at it.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.012
-And I would be clean as hell.

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:08.147
-Yeah. That is a good way of
looking at it.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.615
Think about it.
You think the parents are upset

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:10.949
because they're worried about
their kids' safety,

00:04:10.949 --> 00:04:12.451
but they're just jealous.

00:04:12.451 --> 00:04:14.954
-They're just basically like,
"You spent too much time."

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:17.223
Like, it was just, like,
no cleaning of the house.

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:19.258
She wasn't responsible
for nothing.

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:20.759
-No.
-You need to give that girl

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:22.127
some chores.
-Yeah.

00:04:22.127 --> 00:04:24.030
Rue needs a chore board!

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.931
-She -- Rue -- No.

00:04:25.931 --> 00:04:28.568
Rue need to be strangled
one good time.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:30.670
She need -- her mom need
to grab her and go --

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:33.706
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.710
[ Gasps ]

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.747
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:44.283
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:47.219
-I will say that show is
"Game of Thrones" for parents.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:48.887
-Oh, my God.
-Like that show is way --

00:04:48.887 --> 00:04:51.290
